# Server-side env vars for apps/web/server (loaded via `dotenv/config`,
# apps/web/client/.env.example is separate — Vite only exposes VITE_-prefixed
# vars, and this file's vars are Node-only, never sent to the browser).
# Copy this file to .env — it's gitignored, never commit real values.

# Needed for the Admin SDK's verifyIdToken() to check a token's audience
# claim. On real GCP hosting this is auto-detected; locally it isn't.
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=smartfit-daily

# The Admin SDK also needs real credentials to call Firestore/Auth admin
# APIs — this alone (FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID) is not enough locally. Either:
#   1. Download a service account key (Firebase Console -> Project settings
#      -> Service accounts -> Generate new private key) and set:
#        GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=/absolute/path/to/key.json
#   2. Or run `gcloud auth application-default login` once on this machine
#      (needs the gcloud CLI) and leave GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS unset.
# See README.md's "Local Admin SDK credentials" section.
# GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=

# Optional — see server/index.ts's comment on why this differs from PORT.
# API_PORT=8080

# REC-1/REC-4 (routes/content-recommendation) — GET /workouts/today/recommendation
# and POST .../swap need both of these to pick a real video instead of a 501 stub:
#   1. YOUTUBE_API_KEY — a YouTube Data API v3 key (Google Cloud Console ->
#      APIs & Services -> Credentials -> Create Credentials -> API key, with
#      the "YouTube Data API v3" enabled on the project).
YOUTUBE_API_KEY=
#   2. GEMINI_API_KEY — a Gemini API key (Google AI Studio, aistudio.google.com
#      -> Get API key; separate from a Gemini Advanced/Google One subscription,
#      which does not grant API access) — used to rank YouTube search results
#      against the user's remaining calorie target/equipment (see
#      server/services/videoRecommender.ts).
GEMINI_API_KEY=
